1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,598
Last time your boss was a copy of the Warlord with new names.

2
00:00:05,498 --> 00:00:09,866
So she flew a Kralien dreadnought, with Kralien or Torgoth escorts,

3
00:00:10,316 --> 00:00:12,268
and a corsair shouldn't.

4
00:00:14,068 --> 00:00:17,176
Today you change six lines, one at a time,

5
00:00:17,626 --> 00:00:21,732
and by the end, every number in her file is one you chose.

6
00:00:22,932 --> 00:00:24,939
Here's last time's Queen on Science,

7
00:00:25,389 --> 00:00:26,855
with the Morrigan selected,

8
00:00:27,305 --> 00:00:29,418
her name in red at the top.

9
00:00:30,318 --> 00:00:33,668
Everything she brings is in the first fence of her file.

10
00:00:34,568 --> 00:00:36,742
Trigger says which kind of boss she is.

11
00:00:37,192 --> 00:00:38,777
Low says when she arrives.

12
00:00:39,677 --> 00:00:43,279
Fleets, Flies and Difficulty say what comes with her,

13
00:00:43,729 --> 00:00:46,347
and Named says which ships carry a name.

14
00:00:48,147 --> 00:00:50,230
One thing before we start.

15
00:00:51,130 --> 00:00:53,812
The game reads a boss file when the mission starts,

16
00:00:54,262 --> 00:00:56,525
so after every change you save,

17
00:00:56,975 --> 00:00:58,521
you start the mission again.

18
00:00:59,721 --> 00:01:02,106
You're going to play her several times today,

19
00:01:02,556 --> 00:01:05,214
and you don't want to fight for ten minutes each time.

20
00:01:06,114 --> 00:01:08,909
So set Low to a hundred percent.

21
00:01:09,809 --> 00:01:12,191
Low is a share of the raiders,

22
00:01:12,641 --> 00:01:15,485
and she comes when that share or less is left.

23
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:21,880
A hundred percent is all of them, so she arrives about four seconds in,

24
00:01:22,330 --> 00:01:24,025
before anyone has fired a shot.

25
00:01:24,925 --> 00:01:28,708
That's your test setting, and you put the real number back at the end.

26
00:01:29,908 --> 00:01:34,427
Fleets is the easy one. It's a whole number, written as a digit,

27
00:01:34,877 --> 00:01:37,360
and that many escort fleets arrive with her.

28
00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:42,006
Flies names a race, and there are six that can fly a fleet.

29
00:01:43,806 --> 00:01:45,586
Now here's the part people get wrong.

30
00:01:46,486 --> 00:01:50,556
Seventy-five percent pirate, twenty-five Kralien, with three fleets,

31
00:01:51,006 --> 00:01:53,913
doesn't give you two pirate fleets and one Kralien.

32
00:01:54,813 --> 00:01:56,980
The game rolls once, when she arrives,

33
00:01:57,430 --> 00:02:00,492
and all three fleets are the same race.

34
00:02:01,392 --> 00:02:03,657
So write the mix as a story:

35
00:02:04,107 --> 00:02:06,587
most nights she brings her own corsairs,

36
00:02:07,037 --> 00:02:09,180
and now and then she's hired Kraliens.

37
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:14,355
The crew picks a difficulty before the game, from one to eleven.

38
00:02:15,255 --> 00:02:18,501
Your line says how hard her fleets are next to that.

39
00:02:19,401 --> 00:02:22,190
Plus two is two levels above the game,

40
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:26,317
so in a game at five, her fleets are built for seven.

41
00:02:28,117 --> 00:02:31,893
And the level decides how many ships are in a fleet.

42
00:02:32,793 --> 00:02:35,887
At seven, a pirate fleet is one to three ships,

43
00:02:36,337 --> 00:02:39,324
and a Kralien fleet is four to six.

44
00:02:40,224 --> 00:02:43,428
So the night she's hired Kraliens is the hard night.

45
00:02:44,628 --> 00:02:46,663
Named is two words for each ship:

46
00:02:47,113 --> 00:02:49,509
its name, and then which ship it is.

47
00:02:50,409 --> 00:02:52,395
The name is what Science shows for her,

48
00:02:52,845 --> 00:02:56,171
and once she's scanned, it's her row in the contact list.

49
00:02:57,071 --> 00:02:59,168
Last time you changed the first word.

50
00:02:59,618 --> 00:03:01,554
Today you change the second,

51
00:03:02,004 --> 00:03:04,820
and you add a second ship after a comma.

52
00:03:06,620 --> 00:03:08,857
The second word is a ship key,

53
00:03:09,307 --> 00:03:11,607
and the page has the raider ships in a table.

54
00:03:12,507 --> 00:03:16,972
Type it exactly as it's printed, in small letters, with the underscores,

55
00:03:17,422 --> 00:03:21,905
because this is the one line where a spelling mistake gets past everything.

56
00:03:23,105 --> 00:03:25,325
Lint reads the shape of a boss line.

57
00:03:26,225 --> 00:03:27,685
It knows the field names,

58
00:03:28,135 --> 00:03:29,743
it knows the two triggers,

59
00:03:30,193 --> 00:03:32,718
and it knows a named ship is two words.

60
00:03:34,518 --> 00:03:36,390
It doesn't check the other values.

61
00:03:37,290 --> 00:03:41,530
So if I write pirates, with an S, lint still says clean,

62
00:03:41,980 --> 00:03:45,776
and in the game her named ships arrive with no fleets at all.

63
00:03:46,676 --> 00:03:49,252
Here they are among the Siege's own raiders,

64
00:03:49,702 --> 00:03:51,700
and not one pirate is with them.

65
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:53,822
The game does tell you, though.

66
00:03:54,272 --> 00:03:58,485
It writes a line in the runtime log, in the Legendary Missions folder,

67
00:03:58,935 --> 00:04:00,017
one for each fleet,

68
00:04:00,467 --> 00:04:02,519
naming the race it couldn't find.

69
00:04:03,419 --> 00:04:05,388
And for a number it can't read,

70
00:04:05,838 --> 00:04:09,477
it leaves your boss out of the list and says which line.

71
00:04:10,677 --> 00:04:12,856
Now play it, and count what arrives.

72
00:04:13,757 --> 00:04:15,983
On Science, once they're scanned,

73
00:04:16,433 --> 00:04:19,281
the pirate chip lists the Morrigan and the Badb,

74
00:04:19,731 --> 00:04:21,032
and eight more pirates:

75
00:04:21,483 --> 00:04:23,729
her three fleets, all of one race.

76
00:04:24,629 --> 00:04:27,799
Then start the mission again and look a second time,

77
00:04:28,249 --> 00:04:31,362
because about one arrival in four is the Kralien one.

78
00:04:33,162 --> 00:04:35,674
Try changing one number and playing again.

79
00:04:36,574 --> 00:04:38,643
Set the difficulty line to eleven,

80
00:04:39,093 --> 00:04:41,129
and every fleet is six ships.

81
00:04:42,329 --> 00:04:45,680
Testing's over, so give her the number you want the crew to play.

82
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:48,864
I'm using forty percent for mine.

83
00:04:49,764 --> 00:04:51,470
With sixteen raiders at the start,

84
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:53,960
she comes when six are left.

85
00:04:54,860 --> 00:04:56,338
The crew's winning by then,

86
00:04:56,788 --> 00:04:58,053
but the siege isn't over.

87
00:04:59,853 --> 00:05:03,051
Then bring the note at the top of the file up to date.

88
00:05:03,951 --> 00:05:05,885
It's for you, a year from now,

89
00:05:06,335 --> 00:05:09,759
when you've forgotten why she flies what she flies.

90
00:05:10,659 --> 00:05:13,447
Next time she gets objectives of her own.
